Source: capsa
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Roman <roman@nekko.ai>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), build-essential, pkg-config, cmake,
 python3, clang, libclang-dev, libssl-dev, liblzma-dev, zlib1g-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/nekkoai/capsa
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: capsa-core
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: embedding-based document storage and retrieval CLI
 capsa indexes documents and queries a libSQL vector database using an
 OpenAI-compatible embedding service. This package contains only the capsa
 command-line program; it does not install a service, database, models, or
 embedding credentials.

Package: capsa-federation
Architecture: all
Depends: capsa-python-runtime (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: read-only Capsa MCP federation gateway
 Read-only multi-source gateway using Capsa's private Python runtime.

Package: capsa-indexers
Architecture: all
Depends: capsa-core (= ${binary:Version}), capsa-python-runtime (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: optional explicit Capsa Jira and Confluence ingestion tools
 Archive ingestion entrypoints. No ingestion is started automatically.
 The legacy Drive adapter and missing Slides workflow are not supported entrypoints.

Package: capsa-services
Architecture: all
Depends: capsa-core (= ${binary:Version}), capsa-federation (= ${binary:Version}),
 capsa-llama-cpu (= ${binary:Version}), capsa-embedding-assets-nomic (= ${binary:Version}),
 adduser, systemd, ${misc:Depends}
Description: inert-by-default Capsa serving units and operator tools
 Embeddings, four immutable readers and a read-only gateway. Snapshots must be
 provisioned and registered explicitly. Installation starts no services.

Package: capsa-server
Architecture: all
Depends: capsa-services (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: capsa-indexers (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Capsa immutable serving stack
 Metapackage for the complete serving stack; ingestion tools remain optional.
